💡 Key Takeaways
Subnetting divides a large network into smaller, manageable networks.
It improves network performance, organization, and security.
A subnet mask determines which part of an IP address represents the network and the host.
CIDR notation provides a simpler and more flexible way to represent subnet masks.
Learning subnetting is essential for network design, routing, and cybersecurity assessments.
